            <ArticleTitle>Adult Degenerative Scoliosis with Spinal Stenosis Treated with Stand-Alone Cage via an Extreme Lateral Transpsoas Approach; a Case Report and Literature Review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>124-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 73-year-old female with severe degenerative scoliosis and back and leg pain that was successfully treated with stand- alone cages via an extreme lateral transpsoas approach. This patient had declined open surgery and instrumentation due to her advanced age concerns about potential side effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
